chapter.v:
“Ah, stubborn 


children,” declares, 


the LORD, “who carry out a plan, but not mine, and who make an alliance,(1) but not of my Spirit, that they may add sin to sin;

For they 


are a, 


rebellious people, lying children, children unwilling to hear the instruction of the LORD;

therefore this 


iniquity shall, 


be to you like a breach in a high wall, bulging out and about to collapse, whose breaking comes suddenly, in an instant;

Behold, the 


name of, 


the LORD comes from afar, burning with his anger, and in thick rising smoke;(4) his lips are full of fury, and his tongue is like a devouring fire;
